From: zhzy0077 <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: honor possible_crtcs when allocating planes

The common plane initializer accepts possible_crtcs but registers every
plane with a hard-coded 0xff mask. This discards the Gaokun3 primary-plane
ownership restriction passed by dpu_kms through both plane backends.

On a dual-display Gaokun3 running release 13, GETPLANE still reports 0xff
for all planes, and GDM-to-desktop handoff repeatedly fails atomic commits
with EINVAL. The loaded module contains the board-specific mask calculation
but its common allocator still passes 0xff.

Pass the caller's mask to drmm_universal_plane_alloc so the registered DRM
object exposes the intended CRTC compatibility. This also preserves the
caller-provided masks for physical, virtual, cursor and overlay planes.

Signed-off-by: zhzy0077 <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
@@ -1834,7 +1834,7 @@ static struct drm_plane *dpu_plane_init_common(struct drm_device *dev,
 	int ret;
 
 	pdpu = drmm_universal_plane_alloc(dev, struct dpu_plane, base,
-				0xff, &dpu_plane_funcs,
+				possible_crtcs, &dpu_plane_funcs,
 				format_list, num_formats,
 				supported_format_modifiers, type, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(pdpu))
-- 
